    "b42ab645dd": {
      "id": "b42ab645dd",
      "created": 1795068563.0181403,
      "headline": "24 teams launch Collective Cycling Group, successor to One Cycling",
      "url": "https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/racing/24-teams-come-together-to-form-collective-cycling-group-the-latest-venture-aiming-to-unlock-the-value-of-pro-cycling/",
      "source": "Cyclingnews",
      "image_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068536/cycling-bot/b42ab645dd-0.jpg",
      "image_urls": [
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068536/cycling-bot/b42ab645dd-0.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068536/cycling-bot/b42ab645dd-1.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068537/cycling-bot/b42ab645dd-2.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068538/cycling-bot/b42ab645dd-3.jpg",
        "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/image/upload/v1795068538/cycling-bot/b42ab645dd-4.jpg"
      ],
      "full_caption": "24 teams have signed up to the new Collective Cycling Group. 🚴\n\nThe group, announced on Wednesday, wants to develop and market selected commercial rights to strengthen pro cycling's economic model. It is essentially the renamed One Cycling company, with Oliver Ciesla replacing Richard Plugge as director. The launch statement did not name the teams, and the UCI's view is still to come.\n\nCan teams finally build a better commercial model together?\n\nSource: Cyclingnews\n\n#cycling #procycling #roadcycling #WorldTour #UCI #CollectiveCyclingGroup #OneCycling #cyclingnews #womensWorldTour #cyclingteams",
      "alt_text": "News graphic announcing that 24 teams have formed the Collective Cycling Group to develop commercial rights in professional road cycling.",
      "score": 9,
      "reel_url": "https://res.cloudinary.com/nnmxf7gb/video/upload/v1795068562/cycling-bot/b42ab645dd-reel.mp4",
      "category": "UCI",
      "slides": [
        {
          "title": "What was announced",
          "text": "A press release on Wednesday said 24 men's and women's WorldTour and ProTeam teams have signed up to the Collective Cycling Group, with talks ongoing with more. It aims to develop and market selected commercial rights."
        },
        {
          "title": "From One Cycling to CCG",
          "text": "The UK-registered company is essentially One Cycling, renamed on June 2, 2026. Richard Plugge stood down as director and controlling person, replaced by Oliver Ciesla, a sports marketing executive from motorsport."
        },
        {
          "title": "Who is on board?",
          "text": "The launch did not name the 24 teams. EF Education, Canyon-SRAM and Pinarello-Q36.5 have shared the news. Escape Collective reports 13 of 18 men's and 10 of 14 women's WorldTour teams have joined."
        },
        {
          "title": "What comes next",
          "text": "The UCI called One Cycling incompatible with its governance framework last June. Its stance on CCG should become clearer after the WorldTour seminar on December 9-10, 2026."
        }
      ],
      "background_url": null,
      "text_message_id": 108
    },
